# Python dependencies for this system's write-back components
# (agents/lib/external_write/ and any capability code built on top of it).
#
# Installed automatically into this project's own .venv/ the first time you run
# ./start-session.sh — see the "Python venv bootstrap" section of that script.
# You never need to run pip yourself.
#
# Third-party packages a capability actually needs are declared below this
# preamble, one per line, pinned to an exact version (e.g. requests==2.32.3).
# None by default: a system where no capability has needed one leaves this
# file exactly as you see it. When a capability's code needs a package, it is
# added here automatically -- resolved, pinned, and installed before any code
# that imports it ever runs -- never by hand-editing this file yourself. See
# agents/lib/external_write/dependency_enrollment.py and its sibling manifest,
# agents/lib/external_write/operator_requirements.json.
#
# This file's mere presence is what tells the wizard this system has a Python
# component at all: a system with none does not carry this file, and its
# session startup script skips the whole venv/interpreter-pin sequence.
